   "is_accepted": true,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/47239965",
   "score": 1,
   "created_utc": "2017-11-11T16:08:23Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2017-11-11T16:08:23Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "<p><code>strdup</code> is a POSIX function, and POSIX functions which allocate memory (and do not provide type-specific deallocation functions such as <code>fclose</code> and <code>freeaddrinfo</code>) expect the caller to eventually call <code>free</code> to deallocate the allocated memory.</p>\n\n<p>POSIX does not use C++ memory allocation, so <code>operator delete[]</code> is not correct here.</p>\n"
  },
  {
   "post_type": "comment",
   "post_id": 81430895,
   "parent_id": 47239965,
   "parent_type": "answer",
